# Notebooks are committed without outputs, and CI fails the build when one is
# not. nbstripout strips them on the way into the index, so a local re-run never
# reaches a commit.
#
# The filter itself is defined in .git/config, which cannot be committed, so
# each clone installs it once:
#
#     nbstripout --install --attributes .gitattributes
#
# Until then these lines are inert: git ignores a filter it has no definition
# for, and the CI gate stays the backstop.
*.ipynb filter=nbstripout
*.ipynb diff=ipynb
